## CQ-XAC-01
@group client
@commands Open a world, open the world map over grass, water, sand, leaves, a modded block area; F3+T, look again; `grep -c "Leaked resource.*Finalizer" logs/latest.log`; `grep -i "XaeroAtlasColour\|xaero.map.MapWriter" logs/latest.log`
@pass map colors as before (no gray or black blocks), no mixin apply errors, leaked-resource warnings from Xaero gone (reload-listener ones may remain)
@fails redirect not applied (Xaero updated, ordinal moved) or sampling differs
@reviewed 2026-11-16
shell ! grep -iE "Mixin apply.*(XaeroAtlasColour|xaero)|InvalidInjectionException.*xaero" logs/latest.log
> fill ~-6 ~-1 ~-6 ~6 ~-1 ~6 minecraft:grass_block
> fill ~8 ~-1 ~-6 ~14 ~-1 ~6 minecraft:water
> fill ~-6 ~-1 ~8 ~6 ~-1 ~14 minecraft:sand
> fill ~-14 ~-1 ~-6 ~-8 ~-1 ~6 minecraft:oak_leaves[persistent=true]
> fill ~-6 ~-1 ~-14 ~6 ~-1 ~-8 create:andesite_casing
do {"wait": 60}
key m
do {"wait": 40}
shot worldmap
do {"press": "escape"}
do {"reload": true}
key m
do {"wait": 40}
shot worldmap_after_reload
do {"press": "escape"}
shell n=$(grep -c "Leaked resource.*Finalizer" logs/latest.log); echo "leaked $n"; grep -iE "XaeroAtlasColour|xaero.map.MapWriter" logs/latest.log | head -5; true
look both world-map shots: grass, water, sand, leaves and the casing square in their colours, no grey or black blocks; the leaked count is reload-listener ones only (no Xaero Finalizer lines). `m` is Xaero's default world-map key: if the shot shows no map, the key is rebound in the client's options
